Z||000000||jlhuber||10-30-1999||12:08 AM||||1- how much hp/torque will the stock th125 hold up to?  2- how about if it is modified for street race applications?  3- anybody think 560hp can be cranked out of a 3.1 fiero?  the 3.8L buick GN 270-inch sixer has been know to produce 1000hp without nitrous, instead it uses twin turbos, thus propelling the 3300lb with driver car down the quatrer in less than 9 seconds. with a little bit of work it could be transplanted into the fiero, no?<p>[This message has been edited by jlhuber (edited 11-01-1999).]||||reg||4
Z||000001||terryk||10-30-1999||11:44 PM||||Both questions are a matter of time. How long do you want them to last?<P>The old VW Beetle engine could produce 300HP for at least 1 minute. Enough for a few  runs down the strip.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||10-31-1999||12:43 AM||||CASH $$$$$$$$$ + 3.1 = 560hp. And thats the bottom line!||||reg||1
